  "problem": "$12$ is a multiple of $4$ **and** $8$ is odd.\n\nConsider the compound statement above and the following notations:\n\n- $A:12\\text{\u00a0is a multiple of\u00a0}4$\n\n- $B:8\\text{\u00a0is odd}$\n\nExpressed in symbolic form, our statement can be written as\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}{{field-3}}.",
  "worked_solution": "The word \"and\" is represented by the symbol \"$\u2227$\".\n\nSo, the sentence reads\n\n$$\n{{12\\text{\u00a0is a multiple of\u00a0}4}_{\u23df}}_{A}\\,{{\\text{and}}_{\u23df}}_{\u2227}\\,{{8\\text{\u00a0is odd}}_{\u23df}}_{B},\n$$\n\nthat is, $A\u2227B.$",
